{
  "$comment": "E10-T05 (#5211, BQ-4): one case table for the server's port of the client's binding rules (services/api/candleviewer/api/hotkey_rules.py) and the client itself (apps/web/src/keymap/validate.ts). pytest (services/api/tests/unit/api/test_hotkey_rules_cases.py) runs every case through the server's judge; vitest (apps/web/test/keymap-server-parity.test.ts) runs each against validate.ts, but for the server_only cases, whose rule the client's map cannot express. A letter the browser's Unicode has and Python's 15.0 lacks (U+10D4A, 16.0; U+2EBF0, 15.1) holds the client's verdict, which needs a Node with Unicode 16.0 tables (the .nvmrc one has them); the server is lenient on such a code point, so pytest takes an unassigned one for no single letter (hotkey_rules.py's docstring). Hand-written; no recorded data.",
